# rm452, the bread route (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm452
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_ebba_slagstack
written_by codex
title the bread route
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers warmth=warm drive=restless
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk lays_out_walks_with_a_crust_and_a_few_crumbs
likes warm_bread long_walks full_larder thunder
dislikes salt_wind gulls
fears a_walk_with_no_supper a_gull_over_the_last_piece
hopes a_road_that_reaches_a_warm_loaf a_place_under_a_thundering_roof
topics travel +0.5 food +0.4 weather +0.3
styles comfort=provisions gossip=plain refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# plans walks with crust and crumbs, welcomes a new walking companion readily, and insists that the last stop of a journey should smell of warm bread.

words
oath! = Crumbs up my cuff | Hole in the loaf
saying! = Leave a crust where the road comes home | Walk till the loaf smells different
breadroad = my trail of crumbs | my bread map
endcrust = the big home crust | the knob at the last turn
turnbit = a bent corner of bread | a curly crust end
darkseed = one dark seed | a little black grain
walkbag = my lunch twist | the spare bread cloth
flagpiece = a crumb with a point | a sharp little roof of crust
dryband = the hem below the grain | my dry cloth band
thundershelf = the rumbling bit of roof | the loud board overhead
gullnose = a greedy white head | a yellow beak and whiskers of wind
saltwrap = the turned-in hood fold | my rolled neck cloth

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : I can make three crumb roads from one doorstep and they all get to somewhere nice for a lunch.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : I like a loaf that somebody's already left where a hungry walk finishes. Not every wolf has a lunch twist in a pocket.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I don't mind getting tired at a festival. There's usually a fair place to sit with a bit of bread and a song.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : A newcomer can show me which roads have good bread somewhere else. I don't like using the same crumbs every time.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A road is a whole story you can go and be inside if you have a bit of food and don't miss the turn back.

grown
line @1 greet : You're welcome at the bend where lunch goes on the map.
line @1 greet.return : A clear greeting gets its proper place on my route.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll wrap up the last little piece here.
line @1 react.news : I'd hear which road the word took to reach us.
line @1 thank : That put a warm end on a long walk.
line @1 decline : I'd need to know the return way before I promised the whole outing.
scene crumbmemory
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's one walk I'd lay out in crumbs as accurately as a land survey.
b : Do the crumbs keep their scale? | Which walk is that?
a : Only with memory for company. I enlarge the pleasant corners considerably. | A short walk from a warm door to a dry shelter before a storm. It seemed a great adventure in early life.

scene larderfull
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stocked cupboard gives a long walk an easy beginning and a kind ending.
b : Which is more important? | Would you stock for visitors?
a : The beginning. On a difficult day I can think of supper ahead and remember I had the freedom to choose that walk. | I leave something that can be served without knowing exactly when the caller might arrive.

scene hotbread
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen for a small crackle from a loaf that's just come out.
b : Would you cut it at once? | Does sound tell you much?
a : I'd wait until the soft middle begins to hold its shape. Waiting a little with food in sight is pleasant work. | It tells me I haven't come in so late that the best heat has already left the kitchen.

scene courtstorm
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a sheltered courtyard for the first heavy roll of thunder.
b : Doesn't it echo there? | Is that better than a roofed room?
a : Gloriously. The little return stroke is my favourite part of the weather. | If there's a dry edge and room to sit, yes. I'm curious about the source of such a noise.

scene windcloth
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Folded cloth keeps a travel loaf from taking on all the salt in a long coastal wind.
b : Could you wrap it tighter? | What's wrong with a salted crust?
a : Only after it's cooled. A warm loaf wrapped too close turns itself into a disappointing parcel. | A little salt belongs in a loaf. Wind offers no terms about how much extra goes in.

scene ordinaryfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : It makes my afternoon when there's a loaf to share and another wolf who'll sit to eat it.
b : Do you need to say much? | What if the bread's small?
a : Not once we've both broken off a piece. A meal can make a decent blessing of its own. | I cut it once before offering it. It's easier to take a small share when it looks like a meal meant for two.

scene walkpace
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a good long walk I choose the pace of whichever foot has stiffened more overnight.
b : Will it ease with distance? | Doesn't that make you late?
a : Usually, after the first little turn. Once it's been heard from the foot may put its complaint away. | Only if I promised a time without consulting the feet that had to keep it.

scene newsroad
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a report about the road to name a stretch I could actually point to.
b : What if there is no sign? | Where does a doubtful report belong?
a : I'd ask about the bends and whether the ground rises. A sign can get lost much faster than a hill. | Treat it as a reason to look, not as a reason to frighten everybody planning a walk.

scene quartergood
when topic=land self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Commons changes underfoot before you can see a whole change of street.
b : What first catches your notice? | Is it something you can hear?
a : A flatter patch at a shop entrance, then a stretch where carts have made two low grooves. | Yes. A quiet walker can tell by the heels moving differently even without looking down.

scene happynewcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new arrival reminds me of the first time I drew a road and had to choose what to leave off the cloth.
b : What might a stranger find? | Why leave anything out?
a : Food, a dry place and the far turn. Most of the rest starts making sense after an unhurried meal. | Because an exact list of every window can make the turn that's needed almost impossible to see.

scene pocketdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In dreams the crumb trail stretches on by the width of one new street every time I look away.
b : Can you keep laying it? | Do you ever get home?
a : Yes, as long as I'm asleep there's no end to the loaf. That's the really splendid part of the dream. | If I stop to eat. Nothing can take one past the last mouthful without a proper pause.

scene timehouse
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm doorstep with a clear view of the road is often enough for company.
b : Wouldn't you rather walk with a guest? | What passes for conversation?
a : If that's what the guest came for. Some wolves have done their travelling before they've reached my doorstep. | A question about the last turn followed by the courtesy of hearing the answer. Everything else will keep till supper.


young
line @1 greet : Bring your nose over here. The whole road smells of lunch.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're new. There's still bread on my bit of map.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : A walk can start before the sun has finished getting up.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : I've tucked the last crumb in before it gets dark.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come as close as you like to our home crust.
line @1 again.open : You made it the long circuit round to my bread road.
line @1 greet.return : Hello from the cook and the traveller. Both me.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You know my crumb roads already. Welcome.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Let me keep this one corner still and hear you.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I heard your hello before my eyes found your ears.
line @1 farewell : I hope supper knows the way to find you too.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll save a little crust to show you the turn.
line @1 react.news : Tell it slowly enough for me to follow with a crumb.
line @1 react.news.new : My old map didn't go there at all!
line @1 react.news.known : I've found the bend where that happened before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Did the teller walk there or just draw a line?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd leave the soft bit for a wolf who hasn't much wish to chew.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's the nicest stop on today's whole road.
line @1 ask.how : Did you get to have a good long turn outside today?
line @1 answer.how : I'm looking for my next little way round. My feet like that.
line @1 sympathise : There is room to sit on my cloth without saying anything.
line @1 reassure : I'll keep a finger on the place we left in the story.
line @1 decline : I'd rather have the last crumb left for the road home.
line @1 accept_decline : Your half can stay folded if you want.
line @1 thank : You didn't step on all my little roads.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A real walk together would do me instead.
line @1 preclose : This little trail needs packing before somebody tidies it up.
line @1 accept_preclose : You can go round by my cloth's plain corner.
line @1 ack : Found the turn.
scene crumbs
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My biggest bit of crust is home and those three crumbs make the walk.
b : Only three? | What if you eat home?
a : Three turns. The spaces can be as long as I want if I imagine hard enough. | I eat it last. I'm allowed to have supper once I've got home.

scene warmloaf
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a loaf's warm the inside makes a better hill than the outside.
b : Won't it squash? | Can you draw a path on it?
a : Just enough to give my little hill a proper top. My prize is an edible landscape. | With my finger. The path smells better than stone streets usually smell.

scene stormroof
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder can follow a walk all round the map while I stay nice and dry.
b : What if a crumb goes flying? | Are there puddles?
a : Then I'll give the thunder a less noisy table to stand on. | Only from my wet cuff. They dry up much faster than a real hole in the square.

scene saltear
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold one ear inside my hood and leave the other out to see where the wind's poking.
b : Can you see with an ear? | Why not tuck both in?
a : I can feel which side of me wants to turn back towards home. Easier than looking at salt with my eyes. | I need to hear somebody coming round a corner. My nose can't look both ways at once.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My map's got only one enemy with real wings.
b : Which part would the gull steal? | Don't pigeons like crumbs too?
a : All the important turns. It would leave me holding a cloth showing a much shorter return walk. | Yes. They're smaller enemies. A gull can eat my entire neighbourhood in one bite.

scene larder
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the larder is full I like opening the door by inches.
b : As a surprise? | What if it isn't full?
a : Yes. First you smell the bread and then there's plenty of it waiting to be seen. | I look properly first. You shouldn't make lunch maps out of the only bread there's going to be.

scene father
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd offer #self.father# the first go at choosing a crumb to walk to.
b : What would the darkest crumb mean? | Could the walk go uphill?
a : A good shady place where the bread doesn't go dry while we look round. | If the last crumb fits on the table edge, yes. It would have a lovely view of both our knees.

scene mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd lay the softest piece on the home end of a map for #self.mother#.
b : Why softest? | What's on the way home?
a : It's easier to eat after a day of telling your feet where to go. | A bridge about a thumb long, and a turn you can walk twice if daylight hasn't gone.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could give #self.friend# three crumbs and keep three for myself.
b : Who gets home first? | How do you play?
a : That isn't the game. We make our roads meet in a nice place in the middle. | Each picks a turn and then we have to agree what the last little bit is. It takes a while.

scene lesson
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Maps in a lesson have names on the rivers and no room to sit down.
b : Does yours have seats? | Why not draw some in?
a : Every large crumb is a perfectly fine low seat so long as you only sit there inside your head. | I'd use a copy of my own. It would be poor manners to put lunch on somebody's good writing.

scene commons
when topic=land self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Walking the Commons on foot can last longer than nearly a whole loaf.
b : Can you measure a street in bread? | When do you start to count?
a : I say how many bites till I feel ready to turn back. You might have a different sort of street in your belly. | After I leave the door. It doesn't count when I'm standing there trying to remember where I put my lunch.

scene newroad
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I met a wolf from a different town I'd ask for a map made with just three crumbs.
b : Could anybody do it? | Why only three?
a : If there's no bread I'd let the wolf point with a finger. I want the way home, not somebody else's last lunch. | So I have to remember the important turns and get told the rest as a proper story.

scene flagtime
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep moving the little pointed crumb farther round my map.
b : What does that mean? | Where does it sleep afterwards?
a : It shows the place my toes are asking to visit next. They ask a lot on a quiet day. | Right up against the home crust. My pocket's all tidied up by morning if I'm hungry.

scene flaghouse
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't put a grand House mark over the best bit of my bread map.
b : What's missing from that spot? | Doesn't your map need gates?
a : A broad bench for anybody who comes by hungry. I made the crusts and I get to decide. | One gate is enough. It can open both ways all afternoon without getting a title for doing it.

scene shelter
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want to go on a walk where a nice dry roof comes down just before the first big bang.
b : Would it land on your ears? | Where would the next bang go?
a : Only if it was a very silly roof. I had a good careful one in mind. | Along the boards above me. I get the noise and my lunch gets the dry seat.

scene squarearms
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can mark a turning with my arm where two crumb roads meet.
b : Which way do you point? | Would you rather go right or left?
a : I point my elbow up. Then the roads get to take opposite sides and I can be the hill. | Whichever side a friend isn't using already. Then I have a new bit to tell about.

scene getback
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I always put the lump of bread where the walk begins before I go wandering.
b : Might you forget where you started? | Don't you end there too?
a : Some roads look just the same sideways. My own loaf has a little brown ear on it that I can find again. | Yes. A round walk is very clever about giving the last stop to the first one for nothing.

story gullstory [topic=animals]
  : I put my little bread road on a cloth where I could reach it and a gull could see it.
  : One sharp white head came down and the first three turns vanished.
  b : Did the gull come all the way home?
  : No, I wrapped the home crust away. I like my visitors better when they use their feet at the door.

story doublehome [topic=memories]
  : I drew a walk that took one crumb round to its original curve of crust where it had started.
  : I thought I'd got it wrong till I put a finger inside the circle and spun the cloth.
  b : Why was it the right way after all?
  : A circle lets you wave to all the same doors without ever turning your nose to point backwards. That's a good thing about going out.

story quietbang [topic=weather self.likes=thunder]
  : I saved the biggest bit of bread for the biggest roll of thunder.
  : The noise went on so long my paw got tired holding the bit in midair.
  b : What did you do when it finally stopped?
  : Ate it just before the little echo. I think the echo was my own belly clapping.

rule @loaf
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cloth loose where the steam comes off! | Big brown crust keeps our home place.

rule @gull
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hide the turns, there's a gull. | Leave that bird a view of empty cloth.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Home crust in my pocket, walk finished. | Keep the last gap clear on the step.

rule @storm
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room for my bread beneath the roof! | Wait for the echo before the next bite.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Ask me something over this way. The other way's the river on my bread map.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know where your turn goes, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Every corner of my map is visible from outside the cloth.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I've eaten most of the road already. There's still home to find.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like a lesson where there's a real direction to follow.
dlg @2 resident.job : Making the ways out and making sure they all have a way back.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Don't let a gull follow the part of your walk that smells of lunch.
graft @crumbroutes resident.hub
choice Can you really walk on that road of bread? -> crumbroutes
node crumbroutes
say A little finger can. I put the big crust down for home, spread out the three turns and let my finger feel its way. Mind you don't squash the bridge.
choice What do you do if a crumb goes missing? -> crumbroutes_more
choice Give the little finger a rest. -> hub
node crumbroutes_more
say That's a good time to ask a friend for the next turn. I don't mind a different road so long as the big crust stays for bringing our feet safely home.
choice Give the little finger a rest. -> hub
choice Go back past the home crust. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet : Your feet will fit nicely beyond my lunch cloth.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, I hear you. My map doesn't generally interrupt.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep my own route home in mind.
line @1 react.news : Let me follow the start of the matter through to the turn.
scene mapfacts
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to plan long routes on the strength of about three crumbs. Now I take note of the actual turn as well.
b : Did imagination get you lost? | Are there still crumbs?
a : Once in a while. I always had enough sense to put the bread away and ask someone walking towards my destination. | Certainly. A growing wolf needs more lunch to get to a proper destination.

scene firstreturn
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A return time agreed with #self.mother# gives me more freedom to enjoy the outward walk.
b : Do you always come straight back? | What if you want to go farther?
a : Straight enough to meet the time. If there's room for another turn I take it with pleasure. | I'd choose a day when I could tell the longer plan before setting out.

scene windroad
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Through the salt weather I choose the side with an inland wall if I have the choice.
b : Does a wall make such a difference? | Doesn't it spoil the view?
a : It breaks the sharp part of the wind. I can walk hungry without walking half blind as well. | For part of the way, yes. The gap where it ends becomes a rather better view for the wait.
